  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -442,11 +442,17 @@ LOAD(Y Field):::\n If the “Y Field” is a relative time value, this is the sum of the “Y Field” values divided by the interval time.\n This can be useful for tracking response times.\n \n+DIRECT(Y Field):::\n+Every value of the specified “Y Field” is shown directly. No intervals are calculated and no aggregation function like MAX, MIN, AVG or so will be applied.\n+Settings for Interval and SMA Period won't have an effect on this graph.\n+This mode is usefull for plotting time series of fields.\n+\n Y Field::\n The display filter field from which to extract values for the Y axis calculations listed above.\n \n SMA Period::\n Show an average of values over a specified period of intervals.\n+SMA Period will not affect graphs that are in \"DIRECT(Y Field)\" mode for Y Axis.\n \n The chart as a whole can be configured using the controls under the graph list:\n \n@@ -467,6 +473,7 @@ When using the mouse inside the graph area, either drag the graph contents or se\n \n Interval::\n Set the interval period for the graph.\n+Interval will not affect graphs that are in \"DIRECT(Y Field)\" mode for Y Axis.\n \n Time of day::\n Switch between showing the absolute time of day or the time relative from the start of capture in the X axis.\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
